body:
@gkalpak this is happening when using Angular 1.5.x, typings which have:

```ts
// Support for painless dependency injection
declare global {
    interface Function {
        $inject?: string[];
    }
}
```
which conflicts with `node_modules/@angular/upgrade/static/src/common/angular1.d.ts`, where it has following declaration:
```ts
export interface IAnnotatedFunction extends Function {
    $inject?: ReadonlyArray<Ng1Token>;
}
```

I see 🤔

The latest typings from `@types/angular` should work fine, because `Function`'s `$inject` is typed as `ReadonlyArray<string>`. So, I assume you are using an older version of the typings.

I guess we could change our typings as follows to make it compatible with older versions:

```ts
export interface IAnnotatedFunction extends Function {
  $inject?: Function extends {$inject?: string[]} ? Ng1Token[] : ReadonlyArray<Ng1Token>;
}
```

@zuzusik, @Andy-Blatecky: Could one of you verify whether this change solves the issue for you and if so submit a PR?

@gkalpak proposed code solves the issue

is there any chance to release it as `6.1.11`? 

or `6.1.x` is already frozen?

@Andy-Blatecky: 👌
@zuzusik, according to the [release info][1], 6.x has entered LTS mode, which means _"only critical fixes and security patches are released"_. So, I'm afraid this won't be backported to 6.x.

[1]: https://angular.io/guide/releases#support-policy-and-schedule
